.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="nernst_potential implements E = E^\circ - \frac{RT}{nF}\ln Q. This example checks that it reduces to E^\circ at Q=1, plots the logarithmic dependence on the reaction quotient, and then builds a concentration cell (~chemistrykit.electrochem.systems.nernst.concentration_cell_potential) whose voltage comes entirely from a concentration difference -- about 59 mV per decade for a one-electron couple at 25 degC, as Nernst predicted.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/electrochem/nernst/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_nernst_equation_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/electrochem/nernst/plot_01_nernst_equation`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">The Nernst equation: cell potential versus concentration</div>
